From 0e2a124c0e0e1384f0e4c9ddc4188b48c1b39b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:03:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Add socket caption/typeset and the kernel copy
 \@kernel@@caption

\@caption now typesets every caption through the new socket
caption/typeset {type}{star}{text} (\BooleanTrue for \caption*, the
text without \ignorespaces), after the list entry. The default plug
kernel calls \@kernel@caption@typeset, the previous typesetting (with
the label \@caption@nolabel for \caption*), so the output does not
change. A plug runs at the group level of the caller of \@caption (in a
float the group of the float, with its \linewidth), before
\@parboxrestore, and does its own grouping; \if@captionstar is valid
while it runs. A package that typesets captions completely (e.g.,
caption) assigns its own plug and can fall back to
\@kernel@caption@typeset, which is now documented for that purpose.

Request for comments: the kernel copy \@kernel@@caption of \@caption
(next to \@kernel@caption, the copy of \caption from "Add \caption*,
hook caption/before and socket caption/step"). A package that has always
replaced \caption and \@caption, typically at \begin{document}, can
restore both instead and then use the hooks and sockets; code that wraps
\@caption can call it. It is defined in the release block "caption
interface copies", so after a roll-back with latexrelease it is
undefined like \@kernel@caption. \ifdefined\@kernel@caption stays the
test for the interface. Open questions for the team: whether this copy
is wanted at all (instead of only the hooks and sockets) and its name. A
package that uses caption/typeset can test for \@kernel@@caption, which
is defined only from this commit on.

Documentation: the socket in the steps list, its socketdecl/plugdecl,
\if@captionstar (valid in the plugs of caption/typeset), \@caption and
\@caption@nostep@defs (hooks and plugs see the normal definitions);
clsguide lists caption/typeset among the sockets for classes that
redefine \@caption.

New test caption-interface-007 (default plug, a plug that falls back to
the kernel at the level of the float, a plug that typesets itself,
direct calls of \@caption, restoring the copies after a replacement, a
wrapper of \@kernel@@caption, own \caption with \@kernel@caption*);
caption-interface-002 checks that \@kernel@@caption is undefined after
a roll-back.
